%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Future resource revalidation can roll back provisional specialty writes.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Center Manager
    participant UI as CoachExpertiseFields
    participant API as Express API middleware
    participant S as operationHandlers
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Select active sport specialties for Coach
    UI->>API: PUT /api/v1/coaches/:id/specializations
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorizeExact(MANAGER), validate request
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>S: operationHandlers PUT /coaches/:id/specializations
        activate S
        S->>DB: Begin transaction, read scoped Coach, active sports, assigned classes and substitute sessions
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Reject removal of expertise needed by any active assigned class or future substitute session
        alt invalid Coach / sport or removed expertise still required
            S->>DB: Roll back transaction
            S-->>API: 400 / 403 / 404 / 409
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Replace CoachSpecialization rows and revalidate future teaching resources before commit
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S->>DB: Commit transaction
            S-->>API: Updated specialties
        end
        deactivate S
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error

